		"nodes": {
			"47": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "UV OFFSET\nThe UV Offset node displaces a texture with the UV's of another texture. \nThe texture you want to displace goes into the main inlet. \nThe texture you want to use to displace goes into the offset.\n\nThe multiplier is the amount of displacement that occurs over the X axis and Y axis. \nThe gain acts as a multiplier for both.\nWrap determines whether the texture should wrap.\n\nThe UV offset is a great tool for creating effects that distort or warp the image.\n\nFor optimal quality when working with UV nodes the Texture Bit Depth should be set to either 16-bit(int) or 32-bit(float).\nThe Texture Bit Depth of the patch can be set in the patch panel."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 296.587158203125,
					"width": 872.8341064453125,
					"x": 257.21832275390625,
